+import Mathlib.Basic.Real.Basic
+
+/-!
+# Opaque real arithmetic (port to Mathlib v4.36.0)
+
+This file is not part of LeanCert; it was added for the port to Lean v4.36.0 of this benchmark.
+
+Mathlib v4.35.0 defined `0`, `1`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `⁻¹`, `<`, `≤`, `⊔` and `⊓` on `ℝ` with
+`irreducible_def`. Mathlib v4.36.0 defines them as `@[no_expose] private def`, which hides their
+bodies from importers that use the module system. LeanCert is not a `module` package, so it reads
+the private data too and sees ten ordinary, unfoldable definitions. Its metaprograms rely on a
+definitional test such as `((17 / 20 : ℚ) : ℝ) =?= 0.85`, `rfl` on a reified expression, or
+`whnf (a < b)` stopping at once; with unfoldable arithmetic the same test runs into the
+Cauchy-sequence model until the heartbeat limit or the recursion depth stops the whole tactic.
+
+Marking the ten definitions irreducible gives LeanCert's modules, and every file that imports
+them, the behaviour it was written against. Nothing else of LeanCert changes.
+-/
+
+open Lean in
+run_cmd do
+  for n in [`zero, `one, `add, `neg, `mul, `inv', `lt, `le, `sup, `inf] do
+    let name := mkPrivateNameCore `Mathlib.Basic.Real.Basic (`Real ++ n)
+    unless (← getEnv).contains name do
+      throwError "the private definition {name} of Mathlib.Basic.Real.Basic is missing"
+    Lean.Elab.Command.liftCoreM <| setReducibilityStatus name .irreducible
